# chora_test's manifest (#963).
#
# It holds nothing itself: it finds the network card through the HAL, asks
# the kernel whether the card is claimed, and starts chora on it twice -- and
# once on QEMU's educational device, where the board has one (#977).
#
# 🔑 What it MAY HAND ON is the whole of it.  A chora it starts asks for any
# PCI class, and exec_load() cuts that to these lines (#743): the network
# class, and edu's, class ffh ("other"), each with DMA, registers and the
# interrupt.  So each chora holds those two classes and no other, and the
# second chora on the card is refused by the claim the first holds, not by a
# capability it lacks.

name chora_test
delegatable 5 0x020000 0x7
delegatable 5 0xff0000 0x7
